<title>BELGIUM: EU CLEARS REGIONAL AID TO VALMET UNIT.</title>
<headline>EU CLEARS REGIONAL AID TO VALMET UNIT.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Tuesday it had approved 34 million markka in regional aid to Valmet Automotive in favour of investments to produce the Porsche Boxter model at its plant in Uusikaupunki in western Finland.</p>
<p>&quot;The investment project will help to create 350 new jobs and to safeguard 285 existing jobs in Uusikaupunki,&quot; the Commission said in a statement.</p>
<p>The region of Vakka-Suomi is a &quot;structural change area&quot; which experienced a deep decline in industrial output and the region still suffers of an unemployment rate of 18.3 percent, the Commission said.</p>
<p>Finnish paper machinery maker Valmet said earlier this month its automotive unit had sealed a deal with German car maker Porsche to build over 5,000 Porsche sports cars per year at the plant in Uusikaupunki.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom +32 2 287 68 11</p>
